From dcd8506adcb008413fcdf49e59cff9457ef74562 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:12:44 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 53/54] super-amd: log a growth in place a region behind md

The AMD Windows driver (rcraid.sys 9.3.3.218) goes on with a growth in
place from the region after ProtectStart of the transform log: it takes
that region as done.  mdmon logged the region md was in, so when md
stopped inside it the rest of the region was left without its parity
or mirror copy, and a disk failure there would read garbage.  Seen on
real hardware: a RAID5 of three, stopped midway, finished by Windows -
the parity wrong in exactly the chunks from md's last stripe to the
end of the logged region.  AMD's Linux driver repeats the region
instead (rcblob RC_RestartTask).

Log the region below the one md is in: either driver then goes on at
or below where md stopped, the Linux one repeating a region md did.
The kind of migration comes from the two LDs, as the log is written
when one starts, before the volume knows it.  A volume of less than
one region has none below its old end and cannot be grown in place.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 super-amd.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/super-amd.c b/super-amd.c
index 24d84c0f..002a6f66 100644
--- a/super-amd.c
+++ b/super-amd.c
@@ -4441,6 +4441,19 @@ static void amd_tlog_fill(const struct amd_vol *v, const struct amd_ld *tl,
 		if (v->grow != AMD_GROW_RESHAPE &&
 		    (flags & 3) != AMD_TFLAGS_FROM_END)
 			done -= done % protect;
+		/*
+		 * More capacity in place: the region below the one md is
+		 * in.  rcraid.sys 9.3.3.218 goes on with such a migration
+		 * from the region after ProtectStart - the rest of the one
+		 * md stopped in it leaves without parity or a mirror copy
+		 * (22.11 on hardware, RAID5 of 3: 18 chunks past md's last
+		 * stripe, up to the region's end); rcblob repeats the
+		 * region (RC_RestartTask).  Either goes on at or below md
+		 * then.  amd_reshape_size refuses a volume with no region
+		 * below its old capacity.
+		 */
+		if (amd_grow_shape(v->ld, tl) == AMD_GROW_SIZE)
+			done = done >= protect ? done - protect : 0;
 		start = done;
 		flags &= ~(AMD_TFLAGS_DATA_LOG | AMD_TFLAGS_DATA_PHASES);
 		if ((flags & 3) == AMD_TFLAGS_FROM_END) {
@@ -11132,6 +11145,12 @@ static int amd_reshape_size(struct supertype *st, int vol, struct shape *shape,
 		       shape->size == MAX_SIZE ? ", and no more room where they are" : "");
 		return 1;
 	}
+	/* the log lags a region behind md (amd_tlog_fill): one below the old end */
+	if (__le64_to_cpu(v->ld->capacity) < amd_protect_size(v)) {
+		pr_err("%s: AMD logs a growth in regions of %llu KiB: a smaller volume cannot be grown in place\n",
+		       shape->dev, amd_protect_size(v) / 2);
+		return 1;
+	}
 	if (amd_md_keep_size(st, v, shape->dev) != 0)
 		return 1;
 	/* room for the LD it makes: the records move with the packet */
